course: dictionary
lesson: 3907
title: Frightened: a feeling and a word that changes
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Frightened means afraid or scared. Everyone feels frightened sometimes, like when there is a loud thunderclap at night. Feeling frightened is normal, and it helps to tell a trusted adult how you feel.
explain: Frightened is also the past form of frighten, which means to make someone afraid. «The loud bang frightened the cat.» Here the bang did something: it made the cat afraid. So the word is working as a verb, the past of frighten.
explain: Check the sentence to see which meaning fits. «Mum had been phoning everyone, really frightened.» Mum was not being made afraid by anything here. She was feeling afraid, so frightened is describing how she felt.
fact: Frightened means afraid or scared.
fact: Frightened is also the past form of frighten, which means to make someone afraid.
fact: Feeling frightened can be a warning sign that something is wrong. Get away and tell someone.
fact: «A frightened cat arches its back, stands sideways and fluffs out its fur to look bigger.»
fact: Frightened animals may run or bite, so leave them alone.
exercise: «Mum had been phoning everyone, really frightened.» What does frightened mean here? | *Afraid or scared | Happy and excited | Tired after a long day | Angry at the phone
exercise: «The loud bang frightened the cat.» What does frightened mean in this sentence? | Made the cat sleepy | Made the cat hungry | *Made the cat afraid | Made the cat fly away with joy
exercise: If a stranger in the park makes you feel frightened, what should you do? | Walk closer to see who it is | *Get away and tell a trusted adult | Hide and wait for them to leave by themselves | Stay quiet and keep it to yourself
test: «Quiet patience works better than treats, calling or grabbing» with a frightened dog. What helps a frightened dog make friends? | Pushing a treat right up to its nose | Calling it loudly across the park | *Quiet patience | Grabbing it gently to hold it still
test: «A frightened cat arches its back and fluffs out its fur to look bigger.» Why does the cat do this? | To show it wants a bath | To catch a fish | *To look bigger and warn off danger | To keep warm in the sun
exam: «A boy skipped a lesson, nobody knew where he was, and his mum left work frightened.» What does frightened mean here? | *Afraid and scared | Full of energy and fun | Bored and sleepy | Happy to have a day off
